 "notes": "Fowler, Symmes, Marquis, Boone, May, Wilkinson, Monroe and Manitou are printed without a suffix; 'Street' added for consistency (Marquis printed MARQUIS only). Alley names are printed only in the McGregor-Monroe blocks (LAWRENCE ALLY paste, TUNNEL, PRESLEY); the same straight 20' alleys run the full height of the sheet, so the names are applied at every crossing. Fowler/Manitou is a corner: Manitou begins at Fowler (not on sheet 185) and Fowler stops at Manitou (a fence/boundary line continues south-west, dash-dot boundary 'B'); recorded as T. C.L.&N. R.R. runs in Marquis (ignored); foot bridge over the tracks in Manitou at Marquis."
